d? Action Items need reference case per machine. Use search_cip_cases_batch with machine_ids of all repeated and new machine. Let's call.", type='reasoning_text')], encrypted_content=None, status=None), ResponseFunctionToolCall(arguments='{\n  "machine_ids": "B1_DEVP_03,B1_DEVP_02,B1_SCOP_09,B1_SPUT_03,B1_DSCM_02,B1_SORT_01,B1_RESZ_01,B1_COAT_03,B1_AGST_10,B1_ETCH_05,B1_THKZ_03,B1_PRRM_05",\n  "week_range": "",\n  "query_text": "particle contamination \u6539\u5584 CIP \u6210\u529f \u6848\u4f8b",\n  "top_k": 3,\n  "agent_type": "EE",\n  "use_sparse": false\n}', call_id='call_1549244e3b494118a5dd4960162a5afd', name='search_cip_cases_batch', type='function_call', id='ft_1549244e3b494118a5dd4960162a5afd', status=None)], usage=Usage(requests=1, input_tokens=0, input_tokens_details=InputTokensDetails(cached_tokens=0), output_tokens=0, output_tokens_details=OutputTokensDetails(reasoning_tokens=0), total_tokens=0, request_usage_entries=[]), response_id='resp_2fbc596bb2ce4f2a8e681554b4baf225'), ModelResponse(output=[ResponseReasoningItem(id='rs_aa1ad8ba464645ebab4872343cc6a963', summary=[], type='reasoning', content=[Content(text='We have all needed data. Now we need to construct report.\n\nWe need to interpret trends:\n\nFrom overall report, weighted risk index highest = B1_DEVP_03 (53.7), B1_DEVP_02 (50.4), etc.\n\nTrend: worsening for many, stable for some, improving for others.\n\nNew machine: B1_AGST_10, risk index 28.\n\nRework rate trend: overall rework rate particle: 65.56% (W20), 21.84% (W21), 24.73% (W22), 69.37% (W23). So large drop then rise. PR1 rework rate spiking 108.7% W23 after low earlier. PR2 low 10% this week.\n\nBypass risk: has_risk true, with alerts for PR1 and PR2.\n\nAction items: For each repeated machine, provide suggestions referencing CIP cases. Need to include reference case details: week, actions, etc.\n\nWe should include for each machine a concise action item.\n\nIf case exists for machine (some have exact cases), else note no case.\n\nFrom data, many cases are for other machines not exactly same (match_level family). Should still be allowed? The guidance says only same machine cases, but if case exists but machine ID differs (e.g., B1_DEVP_03 has cases for B1_DEVP_01). That is not same machine. So we must check if any case\'s "machine" matches the queried machine. For B1_DEVP_03, none of cases have machine B1_DEVP_03; they are B1_DEVP_01. So no exact matches. According to guidance: only same machine cases; if none, state "\u7121\u540c\u6a5f\u53f0\u53ef\u5f15\u7528\u6848\u4f8b". So for each machine, we need to see if any case\'s machine equals the machine_id. Looking through results:\n\n- B1_DEVP_03: cases machine B1_DEVP_01, B1_DEVP_01, B1_SPUT_03 -> no exact, so none.\n\n- B1_DEVP_02: cases similar, no exact.\n\n- B1_SCOP_09: case machine B1_SCOP_09 (exact) exists. So we can reference.\n\n- B1_SPUT_03: case machine B1_SPUT_03 (exact) exists.\n\n- B1_DSCM_02: case machine B1_DSCM_02 (exact) exists.\n\n- B1_SORT_01: no exact; cases are B1_SPUT_03, B1_SPUT_02, B1_PLAT_02. So none.\n\n- B1_RESZ_01: none exact (cases from sput, etc).\n\n- B1_COAT_03: case machine COAT_04, COAT_07, COAT (not exact). So none.\n\n- B1_AGST_10: none exact (cases B1_PLAT_02, B1_SPUT_03, B1_SPUT_02). None.\n\n- B1_ETCH_05: case machine ETCH, B1_ETCH_02 (not exact) . So none.\n\n- B1_THKZ_03: none exact (cases for B1_SPUT_03 etc). So none.\n\n- B1_PRRM_05: none exact (cases for B1_SPUT_03). So none.\n\nThus only SCOP_09, SPUT_03, DSCM_02 have exact cases.\n\nWe\'ll generate action items for each machine, referencing case if available; else note none.\n\nAdditional action items based on risk: for high weighted risk (top 3) propose immediate on-site inspection, root cause analysis.\n\nAlso need to address bypass risk: in section 6 mention.\n\nNow craft report.\n\n', type='reasoning_text')], encrypted_content=None, status=None), ResponseOutputMessage(id='msg_b8acae082a78415583b9383f71b0047f', content=[ResponseOutputText(annotations=[], text='### 2026\u2011W23 \u6700\u65b0\u4e00\u5468\u6574\u9ad4\u6a5f\u53f0\u72c0\u614b\u5f59\u5831  \n\n#### #### 1) \u672c\u9031\u8da8\u52e2  \n- **Rework Rate (particle) \u8b8a\u5316**\uff1a  \n  - W20\u202f=\u202f65.6\u202f% \u2192 W21\u202f=\u202f21.8\u202f% (\u8dcc\u5e45\u202f\u201143.8\u202fpp) \u2192 W22\u202f=\u202f24.7\u202f% (\u5c0f\u5e45\u56de\u5347) \u2192 **W23\u202f=\u202f69.4\u202f%** (\u6025\u5347\u202f+44.7\u202fpp)\u3002\u6574\u9ad4\u5448\u73fe\u300c\u5148\u964d\u5f8c\u5347\u300d\u7684\u6ce2\u52d5\uff0c\u986f\u793a\u524d\u5169\u9031\u7684 Rework \u6aa2\u6e2c\u53ef\u80fd\u672a\u5b8c\u6574\u6514\u622a\u4e0d\u826f\u6279\u6b21\u3002  \n- **\u5404 Layer \u7279\u8272**\uff1a  \n  - **PR1**\uff1aW21\u202f=\u202f55.9\u202f% \u2192 W22\u202f=\u202f47.5\u202f% \u2192 **W23\u202f=\u202f108.7\u202f%**\uff08\u8f03\u8fd1 4 \u9031\u5e73\u5747 +30.3\u202fpp\uff09\uff0c\u986f\u793a\u672c\u9031\u91cd\u65b0\u555f\u52d5\u9ad8 Rework \u7387\uff0c\u53ef\u80fd\u70ba\u524d\u671f BY\u2011PASS \u5f8c\u7684\u88dc\u6551\u3002  \n  - **PR2**\uff1aW21\u202f=\u202f10.9\u202f% \u2192 W22\u202f=\u202f75.5\u202f% \u2192 **W23\u202f=\u202f10.0\u202f%**\uff08\u8f03\u8fd1 4 \u9031\u5e73\u5747 -30.9\u202fpp\uff09\uff0c\u672c\u9031\u518d\u6b21\u504f\u4f4e\uff0c\u4ecd\u6709\u6f0f\u6aa2\u7591\u616e\u3002  \n  - **uPad**\uff1a\u57fa\u672c\u7dad\u6301 0\u202f%\uff08\u9664 W21 \u70ba 3.2\u202f%\uff09\uff0c\u672a\u898b\u986f\u8457\u6ce2\u52d5\u3002  \n\n- **\u6a5f\u53f0\u98a8\u96aa\u6307\u6a19**\uff08Weighted Risk Index, WRI\uff09\u6700\u9ad8\u524d\u56db\u540d\uff1a  \n  1. **B1_DEVP_03** \u2013 WRI\u202f53.7\uff08\u8da8\u52e2 worsening\uff09  \n  2. **B1_DEVP_02** \u2013 WRI\u202f50.4\uff08\u8da8\u52e2 stable\uff09  \n  3. **B1_SCOP_09** \u2013 WRI\u202f43.5\uff08\u8da8\u52e2 worsening\uff09  \n  4. **B1_SPUT_03** \u2013 WRI\u202f42.9\uff08\u8da8\u52e2 worsening\uff09  \n\n> \u6574\u9ad4\u8da8\u52e2\u986f\u793a\uff0c\u9664 PR1 \u518d\u5ea6\u62ac\u9ad8\u5916\uff0cPR2 \u6301\u7e8c\u4f4e\u65b