tions: #### 1) \u672c\u9031\u8da8\u52e2 \u2013 interpret rework rate trends, weighted risk, hotspot counts, mention overall trend. Use data: overall rework rate increased from 24.73% (W22) to 69.37% (W23). PR1 increased dramatically, PR2 low. Weighted risk index highest B1_DEVP_03 etc.\n\n#### 2) \u91cd\u8907\u4e0a\u699c\u6a5f\u53f0 \u2013 list repeated machines with occurrence counts and risk metrics. Provide top few.\n\n#### 3) \u672c\u9031\u65b0\u51fa\u73fe\u6a5f\u53f0 \u2013 B1_AGST_10 new.\n\n#### 4) \u5efa\u8b70 Action Items \u2013 for each machine, propose actions using CIP cases. Need to reference cases: For each machine, choose best case (most relevant). Provide reference week, actions, and how to apply.\n\nIf no case for a machine, note "\u7121\u540c\u6a5f\u53f0\u53ef\u5f15\u7528\u6848\u4f8b". But many have cases (some are family but still same family maybe acceptable? The guidance says only same machine ID; however many results are for different machine (B1_DEVP_01 vs B1_DEVP_03). That is not same machine ID, so not allowed. The cases\' "match_level" indicates family or partial. The rule: must only use same machine ID cases. If none exactly matching machine_id, we must state no case. In search results, for many machines, the cases are for other machine IDs (e.g., B1_DEVP_01). So we need to see if any case matches exact machine_id. Let\'s check each:\n\n- B1_DEVP_03: Cases list includes B1_DEVP_01, B1_DEVP_01, B1_SPUT_03. No exact B1_DEVP_03. So no same machine case. Must mark "\u7121\u540c\u6a5f\u53f0\u53ef\u5f15\u7528\u6848\u4f8b".\n\n- B1_DEVP_02: Cases same as above, no B1_DEVP_02. So none.\n\n- B1_SCOP_09: Cases include B1_SCOP_09 (exact). Good. Use that.\n\n- B1_SPUT_03: Cases include B1_SPUT_03 exact. Good.\n\n- B1_DSCM_02: Cases include B1_DSCM_02 exact. Good.\n\n- B1_SORT_01: Cases are for other machines, not B1_SORT_01. So none.\n\n- B1_RESZ_01: Cases are other machines. None.\n\n- B1_COAT_03: Cases include COAT_04, COAT_07, COAT (family). No exact. None.\n\n- B1_AGST_10: Cases for other machines; none exact.\n\n- B1_ETCH_05: Cases are for ETCH, B1_ETCH_02 etc. Not exact B1_ETCH_05. None.\n\n- B1_THKZ_03: Cases other machines. None.\n\n- B1_PRRM_05: Cases other machines. None.\n\nThus only three machines have exact matches: B1_SCOP_09, B1_SPUT_03, B1_DSCM_02. Provide action items referencing those cases.\n\nAlso incorporate Rework hotspot (RW) section: get data from get_rework_weekly_hotspots. Need to summarize top hotspots for Fresh and Rework lot. Use weighted risk indices and avg rework ratio.\n\nSection 5: Rework Rate \u8da8\u52e2 - summarise overall trend with numbers.\n\nSection 6: Rework \u6f0f\u6aa2\u98a8\u96aa\u5075\u6e2c - include has_risk true, detail PR1 and PR2.\n\nSection 7: Rework \u6a5f\u53f0\u96c6\u4e2d\u6027 - summarise top machines per lot.\n\nNow craft report in Traditional Chinese, include specific numbers.\n\nProceed.', type='reasoning_text')], encrypted_content=None, status=None), type='reasoning_item')
